== 5.2 P2 residuals: is the positive bias caused by the extended horizons? ==
   h<=150 only (matches the EXPLORE range) n_slopes=15  mean resid +0.0006  sd 0.0043  max|.| 0.0084
   h=160..400 only (extended)             n_slopes=15  mean resid +0.1479  sd 0.0804  max|.| 0.2570
   all                                    n_slopes=15  mean resid +0.0281  sd 0.0133  max|.| 0.0460
   -> the bias is a finite-size (r) effect: the curve was fitted at h<=150 and the
      statistics still drift with r, so extended horizons sit slightly off it.
